        "title": "Contemporary Science - Replication Crisis, AI, and the Metascience Turn",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Science in the 21st century faces structural problems that have always existed but are now documented with enough precision to require systemic response. The replication crisis is not about fraud — it is about how the standard incentive structure and statistical practices of scientific publishing systematically produce false results. AI is beginning to change the epistemic infrastructure of science itself."
